# Rule 90 — inverses: the deliberately EMPTY slot (ADR 0041 D4).
#
# No named inverse property is minted for any of the 17 relationship verbs (or for any other asserted
# predicate). SPARQL inverse property paths (e.g. `^itpra-o:supports`) already traverse any edge
# backwards without a materialised triple, and each minted inverse would be a permanent published IRI
# that the pipeline would then owe forever — a cost not worth paying without a demonstrated consumer
# need. `itpra-o:meets` (rule 40) is the ONE exception: it is not a general inverse of a verb, it is a
# specific materialisation a consumer's traceability check needs (reading the `Meets:` lines of its
# capability documents against the authored `metBy` edges — ADR 0042 D7) and ADR 0041 D4 names it
# explicitly as the allowed one.
#
# This file intentionally contains no CONSTRUCT query. The runner (`itpra_onto.rules.apply_rules`)
# detects that and skips it, producing zero triples — the slot exists in the manifest, in order, so a
# future rule can be dropped in here without renumbering anything, but it stays empty until a
# demonstrated consumer need is written down.
